ashley_cs: Heads-up: new customer (ScaleQ) onboarding showing websocket auth OK then quick 429s on /v1/clients/preconnect. They rotate tokens and see 401 afterwards. SDK v1.4.2 (browser). Logs below.

raj_dev: paste minimal log and how many tabs/workers are connecting?

ashley_cs: Logs:```
[2026-03-22T09:10:01Z] ws-open id=connA auth=200
[2026-03-22T09:10:12Z] http 429 GET /v1/clients/preconnect x-ratelimit-remaining=0 retry-after=20
[2026-03-22T09:10:15Z] ws-close id=connA reason=rate_limited
[2026-03-22T09:10:30Z] ws-open id=connB auth=401 token_expired
```

They spawn a web worker per document; ~10 concurrent connects during onboarding.

olivia_sre: That's a classic preconnect stampede. The preconnect endpoint is rate-limited. Recommend a per-session shared pool (max 3-4) + jittered backoff and respect Retry-After header.

raj_dev: Sample pattern: reuse a single shared preconnect result per user session, or gate connects with a semaphore. Pseudocode:```js
// single preconnect promise per session
let preconnectPromise = null;
async function preconnect(session){
  if(preconnectPromise) return preconnectPromise;
  preconnectPromise = fetch('/v1/clients/preconnect')
    .catch(()=> wait(jitteredBackoff()));
  return preconnectPromise;
}
```

mike_support: Also ask them to confirm Authorization header usage (`Bearer <token>`) on preconnect and whether their proxy duplicates cookies/headers (can bloat headers and cause auth fallbacks). If rotating tokens, do a staged reconnect rather than all tabs at once.

ci-bot:policy-scan: detected preconnect-burst acct=acct123 peak=11 rec=client-side-pooling

ashley_cs: I'll send the checklist and a small pool example, ask for `curl -I` of preconnect. Customer will try pooling + staggered reconnects and report back in 24h. :thumbsup:
